---
import PresentationLayout from '../layouts/PresentationLayout.astro';
---

<PresentationLayout title="Bridging Museum Collections and Living Buddhist Communities">

	<!-- SLIDE 1: Title Slide - The Three Sacreds -->
	<section class="slide relative min-h-screen flex items-center overflow-hidden bg-white">
		<!-- Background illustration -->
		<div class="absolute inset-0 z-0">
			<img
				src="/illustrations/mountains-sacred-1.webp"
				alt=""
				class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-15"
			/>
		</div>

		<div class="relative z-10 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 w-full">
			<div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-center">
				<!-- Left: Content -->
				<div class="relative">
					<div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded-full bg-[#f5b611] bg-opacity-20 border-2 border-[#f5b611] mb-6">
						<span class="text-xs font-[Cabin] font-bold tracking-[0.21em] text-[#d45c26] uppercase">
							The Three Sacreds
						</span>
					</div>
					<h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl font-[Cabin] font-bold text-[#453c36] mb-6 leading-tight">
						Bridging Museum Collections
					</h1>
					<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-[Cabin] font-bold text-[#d45c26] mb-8">
						and Living Buddhist Communities
					</h2>
					<p class="text-xl text-[#453c36] leading-relaxed mb-6 opacity-90 max-w-xl">
						Exploring how sacred objects, sacred persons, and sacred places can reconnect through innovative partnerships between museums and Buddhist educational institutions.
					</p>
					<div class="text-lg text-[#453c36] opacity-80 font-[Cabin]">
						Tsering Wangmo Dhomkhang<br/>
						Sarnath International Nyingma Institute
					</div>
				</div>

				<!-- Right: Monastery illustration -->
				<div class="relative">
					<div class="rounded-[12px] overflow-hidden border-4 border-[#f5b611]">
						<img
							src="/illustrations/monastery-mountain.webp"
							alt="Buddhist monastery in the mountains"
							class="w-full h-full object-cover"
						/>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- SLIDE 2: The Three Sacreds Explained -->
	<section class="slide py-20 md:py-32 bg-[#f9f2e6]">
		<div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6">
			<div class="text-center mb-12">
				<div class="text-xs font-[Cabin] font-bold tracking-[0.21em] text-[#d45c26] uppercase mb-4">
					Understanding the Framework
				</div>
				<h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-[Cabin] font-bold text-[#453c36] mb-6 leading-tight">
					The Three Sacreds
				</h2>
				<p class="text-xl text-[#453c36] opacity-80 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mx-auto">
					These three aren't separate things in Tibetan Buddhist tradition—they're deeply interconnected
				</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Three cards -->
			<div class="grid lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-12">
				<!-- Sacred Object -->
				<div class="bg-white rounded-[12px] p-8 border-4 border-[#9ed7c7]">
					<div class="w-20 h-20 mx-auto mb-6">
						<img src="/icons/noun-mandala-6259529.svg" alt="" class="w-full h-full" style="filter: invert(87%) sepia(13%) saturate(1026%) hue-rotate(106deg) brightness(92%) contrast(92%);" />
					</div>
					<h3 class="text-2xl font-[Cabin] font-bold text-[#453c36] mb-4 text-center">Sacred Object</h3>
					<p class="text-[#453c36] opacity-80 leading-relaxed text-center">
						A thangka painting, a statue, or a ritual implement—vehicles for study, contemplation, and realization
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Sacred Person -->
				<div class="bg-white rounded-[12px] p-8 border-4 border-[#f5b611]">
					<div class="w-20 h-20 mx-auto mb-6">
						<img src="/icons/noun-lotus-6259531.svg" alt="" class="w-full h-full" style="filter: invert(58%) sepia(87%) saturate(457%) hue-rotate(358deg) brightness(102%) contrast(93%);" />
					</div>
					<h3 class="text-2xl font-[Cabin] font-bold text-[#453c36] mb-4 text-center">Sacred Person</h3>
					<p class="text-[#453c36] opacity-80 leading-relaxed text-center">
						The practitioner or community who engages with the object through study and practice
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Sacred Place -->
				<div class="bg-white rounded-[12px] p-8 border-4 border-[#d45c26]">
					<div class="w-20 h-20 mx-auto mb-6">
						<img src="/icons/noun-stupa-7981677.svg" alt="" class="w-full h-full" style="filter: invert(34%) sepia(61%) saturate(1095%) hue-rotate(338deg) brightness(95%) contrast(88%);" />
					</div>
					<h3 class="text-2xl font-[Cabin] font-bold text-[#453c36] mb-4 text-center">Sacred Place</h3>
					<p class="text-[#453c36] opacity-80 leading-relaxed text-center">
						The temple, the altar, the stupa, the monastery—where objects and persons come together
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Bottom text -->
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
				<p class="text-lg text-[#453c36] opacity-80 leading-relaxed">
					When these objects are removed from their context, when they're taken from altars, from temples, from communities, there's a rupture. The sacred objects are separated from sacred places and sacred persons.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

</PresentationLayout>
